  "VIX9D is not replicated from the stored chain: no stored Cboe candidate expiries on both sides of 9 days: the nearest pair 2026-11-13 (14.5d) / 2026-11-27 (28.5d) would extrapolate (near weight 1.390, outside [0, 1]), which is not Cboe's interpolation.",
  "The stored chain holds no zero-bid lines (two-sided capture), so Cboe's two-consecutive-zero-bid stop cannot trigger: every stored OTM strike with a bid enters the strip, which can only add variance relative to Cboe's rule on the same book; the stored book's own strike range is the binding limit.",
  "The first Cboe candidate expiry after 30 days (2026-12-04) is not in the stored chain (the bot stores calibration expiries and neighbours), so the bracket is 2026-11-27 (28.5d) - 2026-12-18 (49.5d) instead of a <= 7-day bracket.",
  "near-term 2026-11-27: 104 puts / 65 calls, strip K/F 0.444-1.135",
  "next-term 2026-12-18: 122 puts / 74 calls, strip K/F 0.417-1.211; K0 fell back to the nearest lower strike with both sides quoted",
  "Model variance swaps at 30 days (k in [-3, 2], wings beyond the fitted K/F 0.70-1.30 extrapolated, so each inherits its model's wing bias): SVI-cal 17.98, SVI 18.02, eSSVI 17.32.",
  "Gap attribution (VIX, SVI-cal surface): replicated - official = +1.32. Strikes beyond the stored strip would add +0.02 under the surface's wing; the stored quotes beyond the fitted K/F 0.70-1.30 are 0.21 index points richer than that wing, so the truncation figure likely understates. Inside the fitted range market and surface differ by +0.05 (these two terms set the replication against the surface; they are not part of the gap). Left unexplained by the chain: -1.34 (official - replicated - truncation; 101% of official - replicated): snapshot timing vs the 16:15 ET print, stale quotes, rate."
